WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.410
Caroline Aghajanian: On this
episode of "Travel Dares,"

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.110
I'm taking Aj to the
beaches of Mont Saint-Michel

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.510
to learn how to escape quicksand.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.600
Aj Caldwell: And I'm taking
Caroline to La Mère Poulard

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.420
to learn how to make the
world's fluffiest omelet.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.070
Caroline: Come join us on our adventures

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.503
on this episode of "Travel Dares."

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.900
Welcome to "Travel Dares."

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.470
Last season, I traveled all around the US

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.830
with my friend Joe.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.790
This season, I'm taking two new friends

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.110
all across Europe to explore
more exciting activities.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.750
On today's episode, we're
here in northern France

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.197
with my friend Aj.

00:00:41.197 --> 00:00:42.383
Bonjour, Aj!

00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:43.260
Aj: Bonjour.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.320
Caroline: How excited are you?

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.810
Aj: I'm so excited, Caroline.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.750
Caroline: All right, here is your clue.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:48.999
Aj: All right.

00:00:52.107 --> 00:00:53.724
Oh, my gosh, I don't know if I'm ready

00:00:53.724 --> 00:00:54.690
for this one, Caroline.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:57.813
Caroline: Aj, you're gonna
have great time. Let's go.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:02.690
Aj loves unique activities that
are filled with adrenaline,

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.130
and this is one of the
only places in the world

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.623
where you can learn how
to escape quicksand.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:12.380
Before we get to your dare, you
have to take off your shoes.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.255
Aj: Now I think that
sink is, like, a literal

00:01:14.255 --> 00:01:15.875
I'm going to sink.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.492
Caroline: Slow steps,
don't worry, don't worry.

00:01:18.492 --> 00:01:21.146
Aj: What is this, what am
I standing on? All right.

00:01:21.146 --> 00:01:23.223
Caroline: Aj, take off your blindfold.

00:01:23.223 --> 00:01:24.320
Aj: OK.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.100
Caroline: We're at Mont Saint-Michel,

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.268
and we're gonna learn
how to escape quicksand.

00:01:29.268 --> 00:01:32.361
Aj: Oh, my gosh. What?

00:01:32.361 --> 00:01:33.290
Caroline: Yes, yes.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.732
Aj: Oh, my gosh, look at that.

00:01:42.777 --> 00:01:44.540
Stephane Gueno: So, I
am your guide for today,

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.810
and I will show the quicksand
and the way to get out.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:48.643
Aj: All right, let's do it.

00:01:48.643 --> 00:01:50.226
Caroline: Perfect. Let's go.
Stephane: Yeah.

00:02:00.181 --> 00:02:01.930
Caroline: I think we're
getting really close.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.390
Aj: Oh, I think we're here.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.098
Stephane: OK, so we
stop here, and we jump,

00:02:07.098 --> 00:02:08.933
and I will show you how to get out.

00:02:08.933 --> 00:02:09.766
Aj: OK.

00:02:09.766 --> 00:02:10.599
Stephan: OK, and then you can try.

00:02:10.599 --> 00:02:11.432
Aj: All right, I'm ready.

00:02:11.432 --> 00:02:14.115
Stephan: All right, close together,

00:02:14.115 --> 00:02:16.002
jump like this, left or right.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.887
(thudding)

00:02:17.887 --> 00:02:18.720
More, more.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.712
Caroline: Oh, my God, oh, my
gosh, oh, my gosh, oh, my gosh.

00:02:21.712 --> 00:02:24.221
Aj, you looked scared.

00:02:24.221 --> 00:02:25.300
Aj: This is really cool.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.420
Stephan: Be on the side now.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:27.360
Caroline: OK, bye.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.370
Aj: Bye.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.220
Stephan: I'm going down.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.630
Caroline: Oh, no. Be careful.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.230
Stephan: It's, all the water is going out.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.520
And then you have only
the sand around your legs.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.640
And then it's like a concrete.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.209
I try to take off, I can't.

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:42.267
Caroline: You're stuck.

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:43.100
Aj: Very stuck.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.190
Stephan: OK. So, how.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.300
You have to move your legs like this.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.730
Aj: OK.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.703
Stephan: Twist, twist.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.753
Caroline: Twist in a circular motion.

00:02:55.661 --> 00:02:56.494
Stephan: Almost.

00:02:56.494 --> 00:02:57.327
Caroline: You're free!
Aj: He's out!

00:02:57.327 --> 00:02:59.268
And he's out! And he's free!

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:01.553
Stephan: It's your turn.

00:03:01.553 --> 00:03:04.220
Aj: Oh, I'm gonna crush
Caroline in this sand,

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.350
quicksand competition.
I am so ready for this.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.060
I'm really excited,
actually. I cannot wait.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.020
Caroline: We'll see about that.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:13.530
Aj: Oh, yes. Oh yes we will.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.989
Caroline: It's my turn. I'm going down.

00:03:14.989 --> 00:03:16.758
Stephan: OK, so let's go to jump.

00:03:16.758 --> 00:03:18.900
All right. Together.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.627
Aj: Oh, it's almost
ready for you! That's it!

00:03:21.627 --> 00:03:23.409
Caroline: Ooh.

00:03:23.409 --> 00:03:25.727
Stephan: We can help her
to go down like this.

00:03:25.727 --> 00:03:26.560
Aj: Like this?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:27.717
Stephan: Yeah.
Aj: All right.

00:03:27.717 --> 00:03:30.283
Caroline: Oh, it's, my legs are stuck,

00:03:30.283 --> 00:03:32.249
oh, my gosh, I'm freaking out.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.465
I'm stuck.

00:03:34.465 --> 00:03:36.431
OK, start the timer.

00:03:41.965 --> 00:03:43.287
Stephane: And then on your knee.

00:03:43.287 --> 00:03:46.770
Yes, the opposite way.
(laughing)

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.241
We lost her.

00:03:48.241 --> 00:03:49.774
Caroline: You lost me?

00:03:49.774 --> 00:03:52.824
Uh-oh, I'm going down.

00:03:52.824 --> 00:03:54.690
(laughing)

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:57.091
Please tell me what to do.

00:03:57.091 --> 00:03:59.730
Stephane: OK, give me your hand.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.662
And twist your legs behind, twist, twist.

00:04:02.662 --> 00:04:05.190
(laughing)

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.739
Aj: Yes!

00:04:08.439 --> 00:04:10.022
You're free!

00:04:14.882 --> 00:04:17.590
Caroline: My legs, my legs, my legs!

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.069
What's the time?

00:04:19.069 --> 00:04:19.960
Timekeeper: One minute, four seconds.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.770
Caroline: OK. One minute, four seconds.

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.684
Stephane: Let's go to jump.

00:04:23.684 --> 00:04:25.392
Caroline: I'm gonna hop on this!

00:04:25.392 --> 00:04:26.630
Stephan: It's stronger, this one.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.050
Aj: Oh, this is stronger?

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:28.883
Stephane: Yeah.

00:04:28.883 --> 00:04:30.499
Aj: Bye, Mom. Bye, Dad.

00:04:31.499 --> 00:04:33.307
Start the timer.

00:04:33.307 --> 00:04:35.682
All right, all right.

00:04:35.682 --> 00:04:37.476
Caroline: You got this, Aj.

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:39.077
Aj: This leg's almost out.

00:04:39.077 --> 00:04:39.912
Caroline: Please!

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.607
Aj: Ha ha, ha ha!

00:04:41.607 --> 00:04:43.107
Caroline: Your leg is out!

00:04:46.105 --> 00:04:47.379
Stephan: Yeah, not bad.

00:04:47.379 --> 00:04:49.987
Caroline: You can do it, you can do it.

00:04:55.705 --> 00:04:58.150
Yay, that was awesome!

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.328
Aj: What was my time?

00:04:59.328 --> 00:05:00.161
Timekeeper: 40 seconds.

00:05:00.161 --> 00:05:01.544
Caroline and Aj: 40 seconds.

00:05:01.544 --> 00:05:02.983
Caroline: Oh, my God.
Aj: I knew it.

00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:04.810
Caroline: Aj, how did you
feel when you were in there?

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:06.240
Aj: It was a very surreal feeling,

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.120
like I couldn't move anything.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.080
But then when you start twisting,

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:11.310
it really, like, starts loosening up.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:12.143
Stephan: Are you ready to go back?

00:05:12.143 --> 00:05:12.976
Caroline: Yeah.
Aj: We're ready.

00:05:12.976 --> 00:05:13.809
Stephan: OK, let's go.

00:05:15.922 --> 00:05:18.040
Caroline: All right, Aj,
what did you think of that?

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.620
Aj: Caroline, I think that's gonna go down

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.640
as one of the best
experiences I've ever had.

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:22.753
It was so much fun.

00:05:22.753 --> 00:05:24.130
Caroline: Yes! I knew you'd like it.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.070
Aj: Are you ready for you clue?

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.286
Caroline: I'm so ready. I'm so ready. OK.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.010
OK, I wonder what that
means. I have no idea.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:35.683
Aj: I do have a surprise.
It's right through there.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.480
Caroline: Through here, seriously?

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.880
OK, no, yeah, totally, let's go.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.730
Aj: Now, I'm a bit of a food expert,

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.129
and La Mère Poulard is known

00:05:44.129 --> 00:05:46.710
for making the world's fluffiest omelet.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:49.690
Making the perfect omelet
is extremely difficult,

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:52.999
and I'm excited to see if
Caroline is up to the task.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.490
All right, perfect, hold out your hand.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:03.386
Just hold it out. There you go.

00:06:03.386 --> 00:06:05.220
Turn it around, be very careful.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.110
Caroline: What is it?

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:06.960
Aj: Be very careful.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:09.301
Caroline: I'm careful.
I'm careful, I'm careful.

00:06:09.301 --> 00:06:10.343
It feels so weird.
Aj: OK.

00:06:10.343 --> 00:06:11.643
Take off your blindfold.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.740
We're learning how to make
the world's fluffiest omelet.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.398
Caroline: Oh, my god.

00:06:18.398 --> 00:06:22.464
Wait, this is not what
I was expecting at all.

00:06:22.464 --> 00:06:23.412
Aj: You're gonna love this.

00:06:23.412 --> 00:06:25.769
Caroline: It smells so
good, it smells so good.

00:06:25.769 --> 00:06:27.136
This is an egg.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.160
Aj: So, first, Franc is
gonna show us how it's made,

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.680
and then me and you are gonna
have a little competition

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:41.560
and see who can make the better omelet.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:43.860
Caroline: OK, I'm gonna win this one.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.760
I think I'm a pretty good chef.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.210
Aj: I don't know about that.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:50.208
Caroline: Oh, I've never seen
anyone whisk eggs like that.

00:06:50.208 --> 00:06:51.133
Aj: I know.

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:52.561
Caroline: There's a technique to this.

00:06:52.561 --> 00:06:53.394
Aj: Yeah.

00:06:53.394 --> 00:06:54.310
Caroline: It's not how we whisk eggs.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.143
Aj: Yeah, I do a circle.

00:06:55.143 --> 00:06:56.809
It's, like, back and forth.
Caroline: I do circles.

00:06:56.809 --> 00:06:57.990
Aj: Look how bubbly it is.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:06:59.650
Like, it gets fluffy inside the bowl.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.268
Caroline: Yeah, I think that's the key.

00:07:01.268 --> 00:07:03.668
It's like, the harder you
whip, the bubbly it is.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.320
Aj: Kind of push off, OK.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:14.360
Caroline: It's so fluffy.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.963
Aj: Half, look at it go.

00:07:16.963 --> 00:07:20.330
Oh, look at that!

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.563
Look at that!

00:07:21.563 --> 00:07:22.500
Caroline: That's really fluffy.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.333
Aj: Oh, my gosh.

00:07:23.333 --> 00:07:24.166
Caroline: That's so fluffy.

00:07:24.166 --> 00:07:25.678
Aj: It's super fluffy.

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:26.903
Caroline: Can I try?

00:07:28.458 --> 00:07:30.483
Wait, I'm not left-handed, that's why.

00:07:33.147 --> 00:07:34.483
That's so bad, wait.

00:07:34.483 --> 00:07:35.943
Yes, but I'm whisking it, no?

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:39.107
Aj: You gotta give it a push.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.241
Caroline: OK. All right.
Aj: All right.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:45.700
And then scoop, like, half of it out.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.093
Caroline: Uh-oh, that's not it.

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:48.783
Aj: There it...almost!

00:07:48.783 --> 00:07:49.990
Caroline: I ruined it!

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:52.892
Aj: On this part, there you go.

00:07:52.892 --> 00:07:54.097
Caroline: I'm so sorry.

00:07:54.097 --> 00:07:56.347
(laughing)

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:05.349
I'm so sorry, pardon my ugly omelet.

00:08:05.349 --> 00:08:06.523
Aj: It has personality.

00:08:06.523 --> 00:08:08.620
Caroline: I'm sorry, it's like me.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:10.380
You know what, that's my omelet.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.369
That's mine, let's see
what you can do, Aj.

00:08:12.369 --> 00:08:14.011
Let's see your omelet.
Aj: All right, I am ready.

00:08:15.512 --> 00:08:16.945
Oh, oh!

00:08:16.945 --> 00:08:17.778
Caroline: Oh, oh, oh!

00:08:17.778 --> 00:08:18.969
Aj: Don't wanna spill it!

00:08:18.969 --> 00:08:20.880
Push, push.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.171
Caroline: He's really good.

00:08:22.171 --> 00:08:23.004
Aj: Push.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.835
Caroline: I think you've got this, Aj.

00:08:26.835 --> 00:08:30.863
Aj: OK, so I'm gonna come
here and take this thing.

00:08:32.685 --> 00:08:33.602
About half.

00:08:35.655 --> 00:08:36.670
Caroline: Do a little flip.

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:39.412
Aj: Oh, look at that.

00:08:39.412 --> 00:08:41.620
Caroline: I'm impressed, I'm impressed.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:42.634
Aj: I did it!

00:08:42.634 --> 00:08:43.717
Look at this!

00:08:45.083 --> 00:08:46.900
Caroline: This is my sad, you're a pro.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.640
You've definitely done this before.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.250
You mastered the presentation.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.490
Mine just looks like a giant peanut.

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:54.150
Aj: Yeah, I think I did
all right on the flip.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:56.230
Caroline: Yeah, no, but you know what,

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:57.815
it's all about the taste.

00:08:57.815 --> 00:08:58.659
Aj: It is.

00:08:58.659 --> 00:08:59.839
Caroline: So, bon appétit.

00:08:59.839 --> 00:09:00.989
Aj: Bon appétit.

00:09:03.717 --> 00:09:07.070
Caroline: Oh, my God, it's
like chewing on a cloud.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:07.903
Aj: It really is.

00:09:07.903 --> 00:09:09.200
Caroline: Oh, wow.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:11.900
That's probably the yummiest
dare we're ever gonna do.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:14.400
OK, ready to go back to Paris?

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.233
Aj: Oui oui.

00:09:21.184 --> 00:09:22.530
Caroline: We had such an amazing time

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.790
in Mont Saint-Michel, and
now we're back in Paris,

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.720
and it's literally so gorgeous here.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:27.940
Aj: I know. Everywhere you look,

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:30.600
there's just this beautiful
French architecture.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:34.031
But somehow this hotel captures
the essence of New York.

00:09:34.031 --> 00:09:36.422
Caroline: Hmm. I think you're right.

00:09:36.422 --> 00:09:38.780
Time for the rating.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:41.310
OK. I'm just gonna go right into it.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.520
So, when you first took off the blindfold,

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.740
I really thought this
was gonna be the dare

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.880
that you were gonna be
super nervous about.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.530
But it was the total opposite,

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:53.440
you were so excited, and you
also had the fastest time,

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.100
which I was not expecting.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:56.930
I don't know, I just
have to give you a five.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:58.850
I can't give you anything else.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:00.735
Aj: Crushing the dares, I love it.

00:10:00.735 --> 00:10:02.457
Caroline: Crushing the dares, yep.

00:10:02.457 --> 00:10:05.670
Aj: All right. So, for
your rating, Caroline,

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:06.803
I actually knew you were gonna be

00:10:06.803 --> 00:10:08.761
really excited for your dare,

00:10:08.761 --> 00:10:11.410
you jumped right in the kitchen,
you were excited to learn,

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:13.052
you were dancing along to the beat.

00:10:13.052 --> 00:10:14.880
You were having a great time.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.438
But, at the end of the day,

00:10:17.438 --> 00:10:20.600
your flip was kind of a flop.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:23.416
So, unfortunately, I gotta give you

00:10:23.416 --> 00:10:26.257
a three out of five stars.

00:10:26.257 --> 00:10:29.507
Caroline: Oh, Aj.

00:10:29.507 --> 00:10:31.381
It's OK, I'll take it.

00:10:31.381 --> 00:10:33.120
The omelets were still really good.

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:34.340
And I had a great time.

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.690
It's probably one of my
favorite things I've ever done.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.950
Aj: Yeah, and you'll get 'em next time.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.600
